177
00:09:13.540 --> 00:09:17.300
in a democracy. But before the legal effect is given

178
00:09:17.620 --> 00:09:21.560
to legal obligations, Parliament should be able to at least say with

179
00:09:21.600 --> 00:09:24.100
confidence what those obligations mean.

180
00:09:25.400 --> 00:09:28.620
Citizens, businesses, and courts are entitled to know what the law requires of

181
00:09:28.660 --> 00:09:32.420
them, and the purpose of the legislation is to create certainty, not to

182
00:09:32.480 --> 00:09:36.380
institutionalize uncertainty. Parliament also requires

183
00:09:36.440 --> 00:09:40.280
transparency. It cannot meaningfully scrutinize legislation unless it

184
00:09:40.340 --> 00:09:43.960
has the information necessary to understand the legal and practical consequences of

185
00:09:43.980 --> 00:09:47.840
what it is approving. Transparency and certainty certainly go hand

186
00:09:47.880 --> 00:09:51.370
in hand. Without both, Parliament cannot properly discharge its

187
00:09:51.380 --> 00:09:54.900
constitutional role. That is respectively why this

188
00:09:55.240 --> 00:09:59.160
committee exists. They exist to identify uncertainty and resolve it before the

189
00:09:59.200 --> 00:10:01.300
legislation is enacted, not afterwards.

190
