Finally, this bill is frequently described as technical legislation.

262
00:14:10.884 --> 00:14:12.924
With respect, it's only technically drafted.

263
00:14:13.124 --> 00:14:15.064
It's not technically insignificant.

264
00:14:15.744 --> 00:14:19.214
By passing this bill, Parliament completes New Zealand's domestic

265
00:14:19.304 --> 00:14:23.184
implementation of an agreement extending well beyond tariffs, well

266
00:14:23.204 --> 00:14:24.024
beyond trade.

267
00:14:24.984 --> 00:14:28.744
It reaches into overseas investment, immigration, labor mobility, financial

268
00:14:28.824 --> 00:14:31.524
services, digital payments, and future regulatory settings.

269
00:14:32.364 --> 00:14:35.644
It's not about drafting, it's about giving legal effect to international

270
00:14:35.804 --> 00:14:36.564
obligations.

271
00:14:37.764 --> 00:14:41.704
Chair, I return to where I began. The issue before the committee is not whether

272
00:14:41.744 --> 00:14:43.084
New Zealand should trade with India.

273
00:14:43.564 --> 00:14:47.394
The issue is whether Parliament should legislate before it has certainty and

274
00:14:47.444 --> 00:14:50.684
transparency necessary to discharge its constitutional

275
00:14:50.724 --> 00:14:54.324
role. If Parliament itself is still debating what key provisions

276
00:14:54.364 --> 00:14:58.204
require, if members have been unable to find definitive answers during the

277
00:14:58.244 --> 00:15:02.024
scrutiny process, if the committee's report necessarily relies upon

278
00:15:02.044 --> 00:15:05.484
its own understanding rather than shared legal interpretation,

279
00:15:06.014 --> 00:15:08.824
then Parliament has not reached a point where implementation should

280
00:15:08.864 --> 00:15:12.694
occur. Passing legislation does not remove uncertainty.

281
00:15:12.724 --> 00:15:16.534
It transfers its consequences onto someone else, in this case,

282
00:15:16.904 --> 00:15:18.824
New Zealand businesses and exporters.

283
00:15:20.284 --> 00:15:23.484
For these reasons, we respectfully ask the committee to recommend the bill not

284
00:15:23.504 --> 00:15:27.344
proceed until definitive legal interpretations of at least articles

285
00:15:27.584 --> 00:15:30.584
9.2, 9.9, and 9.10 have been obtained.

286
00:15:31.124 --> 00:15:34.164
New Zealand and India have confirmed they share the same interpretation of those

287
00:15:34.184 --> 00:15:38.084
provisions. Independent legal and economic analysis has been undertaken.

288
00:15:38.624 --> 00:15:41.824
Parliament has received a full explanation of financial services and digital

289
00:15:41.924 --> 00:15:44.904
payment commitments, and the committee is satisfied that the

290
00:15:45.304 --> 00:15:49.124
obligations Parliament is implementing are clear, mutually understood by

291
00:15:49.164 --> 00:15:52.934
both parties, and demonstrably in New Zealand's long-term national

292
00:15:53.044 --> 00:15:54.934
interest for New Zealanders.

